WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.135
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy Award-nominated actor

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.705
and comedian you know from such
shows as "30 Rock,"

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.575
"Saturday Night Live,"
and "The Last O.G."

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:11.277
He is currently traveling
North America

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.379
for his "No Disrespect"
stand-up tour.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:14.813
Please welcome back to the show,

00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:16.616
our friend Tracy Morgan,
everybody!

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.619
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:25.892 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:32.165 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.100
Hey, Tracy Morgan, hey!

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.769
We're happy to have you.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.337
It's very exciting.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:39.772
I know you have a lot going on
right now,

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:42.675
but I want to start by asking --
I know you're a lover of sharks.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.944
-Yeah.
-You're a man with a home full

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.746
of aquariums,
and you just hosted

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:49.882
a special "Shark Week" special.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.717
-Yeah, man,
I love me some sharks.

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.186
More than flounder.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.154
-You like sharks
more than flounder?

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:57.123
-Yes! I love sharks, man.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.559
-I never even heard this.
-It's in my blood.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.661
Marine life is in my blood.
-Always.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.896
-A lot of people don't know
that Jacques Cousteau

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.332
is my biological grandpa.
-[ Laughs ] What? Really?

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.003
-Jacques Cousteau!
-You're a quarter Cousteau?

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:12.738
-Jacques Cousteau Morgan.

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:15.741
-[ Laughs ] Really?
-That was his name.

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:18.812
My grandmother did catering on
his boat, the Calypso.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.912
-Oh, wow!

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:21.814
-And he loved
her red beans and rice.

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:23.349
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.119
-Loved them,
one thing led to another.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.420
-Really?
-And voilà.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.823
-Well, voilà --
-They start getting busy.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:30.756
-Yeah.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:32.458
-On the seat.
-On the seat?

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:33.793
-You know, he got a sign on the

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.928
back of his boat that said...
-Jacques Cousteau --

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:37.363
-..."if this Calypso
is a-rockin',

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.865
don't come a-knockin'."
-I didn't know that.

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:43.002
What an interesting
slice of marine history.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.303
-Yeah.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.806
-You -- I want to have
a serious moment here.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.975
I did read that
you were getting a divorce.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.376
I was very sorry to read that.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.645
-Yeah, man,
I'm getting a divorce, man.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.748
My ex-wife took
that social distancing too far.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.450
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.787
She moved out,
and I ain't seen her since!

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.622
I called her up, I said,
"Baby, you quarantining?"

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:06.659
She said, "Call it
what you want to call it.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.528
I ain't never
coming back to you."

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:12.831
-Well, so that is very sad,
but I'm wondering,

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:13.699
are you getting
back in the game?

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:15.868
Are you gonna try dating again?

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:16.935
Are you gonna use
the dating apps?

00:02:16.935 --> 00:02:18.238
-Yeah, I'm on the app!

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.239
-You're on the app?
-I'm on Tinder!

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:24.010
-Okay.
-Tray Bag is on Tinder.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.846
My Tinder profile
is just a Walmart truck

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.048
dropping a bag of money
on my front lawn.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:32.018
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:39.492
I'm holding a sign to say,
"Can I live?"

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:44.631
-Do you -- I know [indistinct]

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.532
I know your ex-wife
was younger than you.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.968
Are you dating women
your age now?

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:52.471
-Yeah, I'm dating
age-appropriate, man.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:54.940
I'm going for old broads.
-Okay. What age --

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.409
-75, 80.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.211
-Oh, you are?
-That's my thing!

00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:02.382
You got pushing around
the oxygen tank,

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.652
you know, she has emphysema.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.052
-Oh, wow.

00:03:07.052 --> 00:03:08.587
-That's what I love!

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:13.493
Organic names
like Blanche or Flossie.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.861
She smokes Pall Mall cigarettes,

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.964
has a casino voice.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.500
She [raspy voice] talks like
this, "I love you, too, Tracy."

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.667
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:27.673
-♪ I see trees of green,
red roses, too ♪

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.309
That's my baby girl.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.144
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:34.747
-Now, it is
the end of the school year,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.615
have you had to
go to graduations?

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.283
Have you been attending
that sort of --

00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:39.619
-I've been to one.
-Okay.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.621
-My Uncle Leonard, he graduated.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:44.557
-Oh, he did? Your uncle?
-In prison, in prison.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:48.528
He did 38 years in prison,
and he's just getting his GED.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.662
-Oh, wow, that's --
-I was like,

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.064
"Well, what you been doing
for 38 years?"

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:55.067
And the warden got these
convicts thinking

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.070
they're gonna get their diploma
and go off to college.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.039
That's not going to happen.
-No?

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.508
-They're gonna get that piece of
paper and go back to their cell.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:05.011
-Do they wear -- Do they
give them the cap and gown?

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.545
-Yeah, they got the cap and gown

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:10.450
and the state-issue greens
underneath with the shackles.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.519
You can see the guard up
in the tower with the rifle.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:17.589
They actually on the stage
singing the graduation song.

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:18.858
Convicts up there going...

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:28.867
♪ How do I say goodbye
to what we had? ♪

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.136
♪ The good -- ♪
They got them doing it.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.305
I just left.
-Oh, you left, yeah.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.840
-It was funny.
-You, um...

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.508
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.376
-Going back on the road
must be nice.

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:38.677
I know people are
gonna be happy to see you.

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:40.246
Are you happy now that
the pandemic is cooling down

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:43.082
you get to go out
and do some live comedy again?

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.583
What are you looking for there,
Tracy?

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:45.918
-I'm sorry.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.053
-I was looking
at the guy up there.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.488
He's not smiling.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:52.291
He's not laughing
at none of my jokes.

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.827
Why are you shortchanging me,
man?

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.129
What have I done to you?

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:59.565
What was you saying?

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:00.733
-Well, just based on that,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.702
we can tell how much
you love an audience.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.904
Are you excited to get back out
and do stand up again?

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.340
-Yeah, man, but now I've got to
worry about monkeypox.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.641
-Monkeypox?
-Yeah, monkeypox.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.077
-You're concerned about, oh,
the pandemic's over,

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:12.078
but you're worried about --

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:13.345
-I'm worried
about the monkeypox.

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:14.913
They're out there!
-Yeah.

00:05:14.913 --> 00:05:16.816
-And monkeypox
has been around forever.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:17.783
-Oh, it's not new.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.151
-It's been around
since the '90s.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.620
-Really?
-They ain't nothing but clap.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.022
-What?
-The monkeypox --

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:26.592
my cousin, Bernard,
he got the monkeypox in '96.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.161
-Oh, wow.
-Well, he had gonorrhea, too,

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.796
so they just gave him
a shot of penicillin

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.296
and got rid of both of them.

00:05:31.296 --> 00:05:32.431
-Oh, they knocked them out
at once.

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:33.633
That's nice. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.068
-One shot for the price of --
-Monkeypox.

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:37.136
That's the reason why Michael
Jackson got rid of Bubbles.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.272
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.140
Bubbles gave him monkeypox.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.942
Bubbles was a nasty chimp.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.076
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:46.512
He hit anything moving.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:49.282
-Yeah, you know what?
We don't hear a lot about --

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:51.517
-Bubbles was nasty!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.619
He can't come to my house.
-Bubbles can't --

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:57.957
-He better stay away
from my sister, I know that.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:02.795
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:05.031
-We'll be right back
with more from Tracy Morgan.

